      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bon Air’s name comes from the French phrase meaning “good air,” a nod to its early reputation as a health resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon_Air%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The central part of Bon Air is a National Historic District, showcasing Victorian homes from the late 1800s and early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon_Air%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every May, Bon Air hosts a Victorian Days parade, celebrating its resort‑era architecture and community spirit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon_Air%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Until passenger service ended in 1957, Bon Air boasted three railroad stops within a mile of each other.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon_Air%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
